-- title:
--   Annihilator of local translates of a cuspidal GL₃ eigenform
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a finite set of finite places of $\mathbb{Q}$, let $\omega$ be a homomorphism from the idele group of $\mathbb{Q}$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, and let $\lambda_1,\lambda_2$ be complex-valued functions on the finite places. Let $f\colon GL_3(\mathbb{A}) \to \mathbb{C}$ be continuous, invariant on the left under $GL_3(\mathbb{Q})$ embedded entrywise, satisfying $f(zg)=\omega(z)f(g)$ for every scalar matrix $z$ with $z$ an idele unit, of moderate growth in the sense that $\|f(g)\| \le C\,\mathrm{gauge}_3(g)^N$ for some $C$ and $N$, and cuspidal along both standard maximal parabolics: for every $g$ the double integrals of $f(u\,g)$ over $u=$ `radicalP21` $(x,y)$ and $u=$ `radicalP12` $(x,y)$ vanish, the integrations being with respect to the additive Haar measure on the adeles conditioned on the adelic box (the carrier pins here being `productionPinsOf` with empty domain, trivial level subgroups and trivial generators). Assume further that for each $p \notin S$ the function $f$ is right invariant under the image of the local maximal compact `localMaximalCompact3` at $p$, and is a coset eigenfunction there with eigenvalue $\lambda_1(p)$ for the generator $\mathrm{diag}(\varpi,1,1)$ and $\lambda_2(p)$ for $\mathrm{diag}(\varpi,\varpi,1)$, meaning that for every finite system of representatives satisfying `IsHeckeCosetSystem` the sum of $f$ over the corresponding right cosets equals the eigenvalue times $f$. Let $v$ be a finite place and suppose $f$ is fixed on the right by an open subgroup of $GL_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ embedded at $v$. Then there exist a complex vector space $E$ and a monoid homomorphism $\pi_E \colon GL_3(\mathbb{Q}_v) \to \mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(E)$ which is irreducible ($E \neq 0$ and every $\pi_E$-stable submodule is $\bot$ or $\top$), smooth (every vector has open stabiliser) and admissible (the fixed space of every compact open subgroup is finite-dimensional), together with $d \in \mathbb{N}$ and vectors $e_1,\dots,e_d \in E$, such that for every finitely supported $\mu \colon GL_3(\mathbb{Q}_v) \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\sum_h \mu(h)\,\pi_E(h)e_j = 0$ for all $j$ one has $\sum_h \mu(h)\,\bigl(g \mapsto f(g\,h_v)\bigr) = 0$, where $h_v$ denotes the image of $h$ in $GL_3(\mathbb{A})$.
--
--   This is the local statement, at a single finite place, that the space of right translates of a cuspidal Hecke eigenform on $GL_3$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ is annihilated by the annihilator of a finite family of vectors in one irreducible smooth admissible representation of $GL_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$; equivalently, the representation generated by $f$ under right translation at $v$ is a quotient of a finitely generated submodule of a power of $E$. It is used by [`LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.exists_sum_eq_span_translates_of_isCuspidalAlong_of_isCosetEigenfunction`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.exists_sum_eq_span_translates_of_isCuspidalAlong_of_isCosetEigenfunction) in the analysis of the local components of the automorphic representation attached to such an eigenform.
